{"name":"Roycroft Vellum","hex":"#e8d9bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vellum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of parchment paper made from the skin of a lamb, baby goat, or calf.","A writing paper of very high quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vellum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roycroft","blocks":[{"text":"Roycroft was a reformist community of craft workers and artists which formed part of the Arts and Crafts movement in the United States. Elbert Hubbard founded the community in 1895, in the village of East Aurora, New York, near Buffalo. Participants were known as Roycrofters. The work and philosophy of the group, often referred to as the Roycroft movement, had a strong influence on the development of American architecture and design in the early 20th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg/330px-Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roycroft"},{"title":"Vellum","blocks":[{"text":"Vellum is prepared animal skin or membrane, typically used as writing material. It is often distinguished from parchment, either by being made from calfskin, rather than the skin of other animals, or simply by being of a higher quality. Vellum is prepared for writing and printing on single pages, scrolls, and codices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Magna_Carta_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Augustus_II.106%29.jpg/330px-Magna_Carta_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Augustus_II.106%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vellum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/500px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.